    "created_at": "2016-07-19T17:09:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-19T18:24:46Z",
    "body": "I picked up the term \"bad frame\" from the [Intent to Deprecate: overflowchanged event](https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/d/msg/blink-dev/1RCzsyEyNU8/gs7gLOjIU78J) on blink-dev two years ago, I don't know if this is what it's usually called.\n\nBut let me illustrate it with commented code:\n\n``` JavaScript\nscreen.orientation.addEventListener('change', function() {\n  // called in the first animation frame task after the user rotates\n  // the viewport width and height have changed\n  // there will be a layout before the next paint\n  someElement.requestFullscreen();\n  document.addEventListener('fullscreenchange', function() {\n    // called in the first animation frame task after going fullscreen\n    // the viewport size (most likely height) has changed again\n    // there will be a layout before the next paint\n    // probably some things will move vertically\n  });\n});\n```\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
